---
system: sys-20-content-authoring-review
flow_id: template-safety-screen-to-publish
surface: internal-RPC
spec_anchor: /software/systems/20-content-authoring-review#template-lifecycle-state-machine
actors: [AuthoringConsole, AuthoringService, PostgreSQL, SQS, SafetyScreener, ClaudeHaiku, ReviewerConsole]
apis:
  - POST /internal/v1/authoring/templates/:id/submit-for-review
  - POST /internal/v1/authoring/reviews/:id/approve
  - POST /internal/v1/authoring/reviews/:id/request-changes
externals: [SQS, ClaudeHaiku]
queues:
  - ca-safety-screen
  - ca-quality-score
failure_paths:
  - draft_validation_failure
  - blocklist_match
  - llm_safety_flagged
  - pii_detected
  - reviewer_role_insufficient
  - quality_score_timeout
idempotency: state machine guards transitions (draft→safety_screening→in_review→approved); safety screen per template_version
retry: SQS retry 3x with backoff; failed safety auto-transitions to changes_requested
timeout: 30s safety-screen — 45s quality-score per job
status: final
---
%% HAND-CURATED. sys-20 has zero seed — composed from spec §5 + §7 queue pipeline.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant AuthoringConsole
    participant AuthoringService
    participant PostgreSQL
    participant SQS as SQS ca-safety-screen / ca-quality-score
    participant SafetyScreener
    participant ClaudeHaiku
    participant ReviewerConsole

    AuthoringConsole->>AuthoringService: POST /internal/v1/authoring/templates/:id/submit-for-review

    alt draft_validation_failure
        Note over AuthoringService: templateText 10-500 chars, variationInstruction 10-300, ≥1 age band
        AuthoringService-->>AuthoringConsole: 422 draft_validation_failure
    else accepted
        AuthoringService->>PostgreSQL: UPDATE ca_authoring_templates SET status='safety_screening' WHERE id=$1
        AuthoringService->>SQS: enqueue ca-safety-screen {template_id, version}
        AuthoringService-->>AuthoringConsole: 202 {status: safety_screening}

        SQS->>SafetyScreener: deliver (timeout 30s)
        SafetyScreener->>PostgreSQL: SELECT template_text, variation_instruction
        SafetyScreener->>SafetyScreener: blocklist regex check (sys-05)
        alt blocklist_match
            SafetyScreener->>PostgreSQL: INSERT ca_safety_screen_results {pass:false, reason: blocklist}
            SafetyScreener->>PostgreSQL: UPDATE template SET status='changes_requested'
        else passes_blocklist
            SafetyScreener->>ClaudeHaiku: classify(template_text, variation_instruction, policy)
            alt llm_safety_flagged
                ClaudeHaiku-->>SafetyScreener: {safe: false, flagged_categories: [...]}
                SafetyScreener->>PostgreSQL: INSERT ca_safety_screen_results {pass:false, reason: llm_flagged}
                SafetyScreener->>PostgreSQL: UPDATE template SET status='changes_requested'
            else llm_safe
                ClaudeHaiku-->>SafetyScreener: {safe: true}
                SafetyScreener->>SafetyScreener: PII regex (email, phone, address, name)
                alt pii_detected
                    SafetyScreener->>PostgreSQL: INSERT ca_safety_screen_results {pass:false, reason: pii}
                    SafetyScreener->>PostgreSQL: UPDATE template SET status='changes_requested'
                else all_passed
                    SafetyScreener->>PostgreSQL: INSERT ca_safety_screen_results {pass:true}
                    SafetyScreener->>PostgreSQL: UPDATE template SET status='in_review' and auto-assign reviewer
                    SafetyScreener->>SQS: enqueue ca-quality-score {template_id}
                    alt quality_score_timeout
                        Note over SQS,ClaudeHaiku: > 45s — message returns to queue (max 3 retries)
                    else scored
                        Note over PostgreSQL: ca_quality_scores row written (advisory only)
                    end
                end
            end
        end

        ReviewerConsole->>AuthoringService: POST /internal/v1/authoring/reviews/:id/approve
        alt reviewer_role_insufficient
            AuthoringService-->>ReviewerConsole: 403 (need content_reviewer or content_admin)
        else approved
            AuthoringService->>PostgreSQL: UPDATE template SET status='approved'
            AuthoringService-->>ReviewerConsole: 200 approved
        end
    end

    Note over AuthoringConsole,ReviewerConsole: safety gates human review (advisory quality score) — every version immutable once submitted — published only by content_admin
